# EXPERIMENTAL REFERENCE ONLY
#
# Do not copy this file directly into /boot/firmware/config.txt.
# Validate the current Raspberry Pi OS KMS/DPI configuration syntax, GPIO
# mapping, signal polarity, and electrical interface before experimenting.
#
# The numbers below describe the target raster model:
#   active:       512 x 342
#   total:        approximately 704 x 370
#   pixel clock:  approximately 15.67 MHz
#   refresh:      approximately 60.15 Hz
#
# A legacy firmware-style timing model would be shaped approximately like:
#
# dtoverlay=dpi24
# enable_dpi_lcd=1
# display_default_lcd=1
# dpi_group=2
# dpi_mode=87
# dpi_timings=15670000 512 32 128 32 342 11 3 14 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
#
# The exact dpi_timings field order and output-format value are platform and
# firmware dependent. KMS may require a video= or custom DRM mode instead.
# This project will not apply boot settings automatically.
